# F7 L2c — Prelude section-composition aliases per spec §4.10.2.
#
# `data:`  primitive-composed as: runtime immutable identity.
#          Fields inside `data:` are per-instance, immutable after init,
#          participate in structural equality / hash / copy — the record
#          canonical shape.
#
# `static:` primitive-composed as: compile_time immutable.
#           Fields inside `static:` are per-type, allocated once, immutable.
#
# Not shipped here:
# - `state:` — retired at v1.0 per §1.11 (all fields are `data:`; mutation
#             flows through transitions). The parser hard-rejects `state:`
#             with a targeted diagnostic; adding it as an alias would
#             contradict the retirement.
# - `methods:` — retired at v1.0 per F67 L4 (Proposal G class-body
#                collapse; top-level callables are the spec-canonical form).

alias data: runtime immutable identity
alias static: compile_time immutable
